# `given || (() => late)`: what is called is the closure of the program or whatever `given` was. What has escaped is among what is unseen, so the settled type of the callee names no function (LinkFlow::settleTypes()).
# The order in which a program starts took such a call for one of unseen code that holds nothing of the program yet, which enters nothing. So nobody entered the closure in front of the store,
# `late` lost its `absent`, and the read in the dead zone gave undefined where it throws a ReferenceError
# RUN: link variables mechanisms=all
# CHECK: variable g0 proven=i32|absent
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# NONE: ReferenceError
# NONE-NEXT: 1
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(ALL): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ALL: ReferenceError
# ALL-NEXT: 1
# ALL-NEXT: exited with 0
# -- source: main.mjs
